# Screenshots written beside the working tree. Two have been committed by
# accident and removed again (e0d7e78, and the commit before this one): a
# capture lands in the repository root whenever a tool is pointed at a
# relative path before its output directory exists, and `git add -A` takes
# it from there. Root level only — docs and the console keep their images
# in directories, and those are still tracked.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# The devenv's generated run directory (ADR-0052): composed supervisor
# configs, the live snapshot, and container state. Everything in it is
# rebuilt by `devenv/devenv up`.
devenv/run/

# Python bytecode from the pack generator (docs/branding/pack/tools/).
__pycache__/

# Build output from the repository's own tools. `go build ./tools/docslint`
# drops a `docslint` executable in whatever directory it is run from, which
# for these is the repository root, and one of those (`vendorlint`) was
# committed and lived in the tree for the whole of the build (issue #122).
# The tools are invoked with `go run`, so nothing needs the file. Anything
# these lines miss is caught by `go run ./tools/binlint`, which fails on any
# tracked file that is a compiled executable.
/binlint
/docslint
/vendorlint
